<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sphrāgis</span></b> , īdis,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφραγίς</span> (a seal).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of stone used for seals</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				8, 37, § 117</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Another name for <i>Lemnian earth</i>, so called because sold in sealed packets,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				35, 6, 14, § 33</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A little ball of plaster</i> in medicine, <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
				26, 23</span></i> (5, 20, 2, written as Greek).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
